## Analysis of Prior Observations

**Key trends for Elastic Modulus (maximize):**

| Exp | Speed | Bath T | Wait | NIPS time | N₂ | EM (MPa) | Strain@50bar | CV |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 10 | 5 | 30 | 125 | Y | 199.9 | 0.328 | 0.065 |
| 2 | 15 | 5 | 30 | 1200 | Y | 226.8 | 0.280 | 0.048 |
| 3 | 20 | 5 | 30 | 1800 | Y | 204.8 | 0.461 | 0.064 |
| 4 | 12 | 5 | 15 | 1800 | Y | 171.4 | 0.455 | 0.082 |
| 5 | 15 | 10 | 30 | 1200 | Y | 229.2 | 0.305 | 0.085 |
| 6 | 17 | 5 | 30 | 1200 | Y | 257.2* | 0.409 | 0.089 |

*Exp 6 had a discarded fit (38/100 quality) — the EM value is unreliable.

**Reliable best:** Exp 5 (bath=10°C, speed=15, wait=30s, NIPS=1200s): EM=229.2, Strain=0.305, CV=0.085 — but high CV.
**Second best reliable:** Exp 2 (bath=5°C, speed=15, wait=30s, NIPS=1200s): EM=226.8, Strain=0.280, CV=0.048 — best CV and lowest strain.

**Key observations:**
- Speed=15, wait=30s, NIPS=1200s is a consistently strong combination
- Bath=10°C vs 5°C at speed=15 gives slightly higher EM but worse CV and higher strain
- Longer NIPS time (1800s) at speed=20 didn't help EM and worsened strain
- Shorter wait (15s) hurt EM
- The 30s N₂ purge appears consistently beneficial
- All membranes show top-gap coverage defects — this appears systematic and not parameter-dependent in the tested range

**Next experiment rationale:**
- Anchor the best reliable conditions: speed=15, wait=30s, N₂=True, NIPS=1200s
- Try bath_temp=15°C — slightly warmer than 10°C to test if the trend (5→10°C improves EM) continues, while potentially reducing strain
- Keep polymer_wt=17 (max, locked at 25°C mixing)
